  "argument_conclusions": [
    "Production PlaceNew <generated OLB path> C2053170_STM32F031F6P7TR 0 matches installed official examples; no observed argument-count mismatch.",
    "The package exists and independent OLB enumeration finds exactly one package, device and logical part, with 20 pins.",
    "Earlier GetDesignator values matched (-1); initial GetId scans did not inspect status. The follow-up returned GetId=0 with Failed=1, so IDs are unavailable rather than valid zero IDs. See v0.49.1-capture-placement.json.",
    "The third PlaceNew argument is named flag in the official wrapper. The available official sources do not establish that it should be replaced by the native device designator or an assumed device index.",
    "The official PlacePartEx example provides a separate designator slot; it must not be used to infer PlaceNew argument semantics by position."
  ],
  "evidence_boundaries": [
    "Both dumps prove a native null read in the same module/RVA while constructing a placed instance. They do not identify the invalid native object's origin or whether product state, loaded libraries, callback timing, or a host defect triggered it.",
    "TclChannelEventScriptInvoker and Tcl_NotifyChannel occur below Capture in both interrupted stacks, consistent with the product's fileevent -> finish -> PlaceNew path. This is context, not proof that fileevent or execution traces caused the crash.",
    "Large symbol offsets in the report may reflect the nearest exported symbol; private debug symbols are unavailable. The dump-derived module/RVA and exception parameters are stronger location evidence than inferred private function names.",
    "Initial instrumented trial compiled a new OLB immediately before PlaceNew; successful repeats used the cached file in a different Capture session. Trace presence, first-load/build state and process state were not isolated one variable at a time.",
    "The saved session log reports the not-yet-existing target OLB, then creates and saves it; those lines alone are not evidence of a missing library at placement time.",
    "The confirmed hostedClientId QA callback mismatch is separate: the crashes occur before PlaceNew returns; callback adjustment does not explain these crashes."
  ],
  "conclusion": "Fault module and exception are now established. Root cause remains unproven. Do not modify geometry, device metadata, license handling or PlaceNew arguments based only on these observations.",
